+# npm assessment for selected Builds 4.39.0
+
+**Security remains unresolved.** The refreshed exact-lock audit exits **1**: **37 moderate and one high dependency entry**, representing **eight unique advisories**. Every affected installed version matches its locked version. [All 38 dependency paths](affected-dependency-paths.json), [per-advisory analysis](applicability.json), [audit receipt](audit-locked.command.json), [raw audit](audit-locked.stdout.log), and [official advisory ranges](official-advisory-observations.json) retain the actual inputs/results. Signature success and successful publication do not resolve this audit.
+
+Source is `2186b9a4bc507a116a457c590c80945c2e232cbd`. Selected package.json SHA-256 is `6b24b99692d3ea18a3554e6018a271b951bd5a4c83db5895e1a83a98218d61a9`; package-lock.json SHA-256 is `1ff1ac5a67d88d1c16eb10ac4b861e989d5c9c629f73a461ccc151c1f7e87724`. The copied installed tree passes `npm ls --all --json`. Both selected dependency files and the original installed tree are preserved; experiments use command-owned `/tmp` copies.
+
+The four affected leaves are bundled under installed npm 11.21.1, reached through semantic-release 25.0.9 -> @semantic-release/npm 13.2.0 -> npm. The [installed source observations](executable-source-observations.json) bind actual call-site bytes. npm audit signatures under installed npm 11.21.1 passes **495 signatures and 130 attestations**, while its [module-resolution trace](npm-signature-modules.jsonl) records glob/minimatch/SOCKS/ip-address paths and **no bundled undici path**. The trace records resolution, including require.resolve; it does not establish sink invocation or safe sink inputs.
+
+| Advisory | Affected installed leaf; official first fixed version | Actual use and limit |
