+| [GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4) | glob 13.0.6; `>=9.0.0 <=14.0.1` -> 14.0.2 | Aborted traversal can continue reading directories. npm commands resolve this module through map-workspaces/package-json/cacache. Selected root has no workspaces; reviewed npm callers do not pass an AbortSignal. Absence of an observed abort is not a general nonreachability proof. Insufficient proof for a blanket vulnerability pass; affected on disk. |
+| [GHSA-rxp7-6hxx-x8q5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rxp7-6hxx-x8q5) | ip-address 10.7.2; `<=10.7.3` -> 10.7.4 | npm network helpers resolve socks-proxy-agent -> socks -> ip-address. Observed socks Address6 calls use fromByteArray over an exactly 16-byte SOCKS reply, and outbound IPv6 is screened by net.isIPv6; that path does not feed an unbounded zone string into Address6. Generic Address6 APIs remain vulnerable. No vulnerable string path found in inspected SOCKS calls; affected on disk. |
+| [GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249) | minimatch 10.2.5; `<11.0.1` -> 11.0.1 | glob forces optimizationLevel=2, the affected preprocessing mode. Other npm callers and TUF/ignore filtering also use minimatch. Exact root has no workspaces and no hostile pattern was observed, but package/workspace/glob inputs require stronger trust proof. Module-load tracing cannot establish that proof. Potential executable path remains unresolved; fail closed. |
+| [GHSA-4qv8-2p9j-2685](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4qv8-2p9j-2685) | undici 6.29.0; `>=6.5.0 <6.29.1` -> 6.29.1 | Bundled undici is imported by node-gyp/download.js, which uses Agent/EnvHttpProxyAgent/RetryAgent/fetch. It does not use EventSource. Actual configured GitHub plugin resolves to external undici 7.30.1. No EventSource constructor occurs in inspected selected command paths. Feature not observed in selected paths; affected on disk. |
